# A continuation line inside an unclosed `(` is not a new statement; the error points at the end (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
from T | where f(a,
b
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..22
  PIPELINE@0..21
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "T"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..21
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      CALL_EXPR@15..21
        NAME_REF@15..16
          IDENT@15..16 "f"
        ARG_LIST@16..21
          L_PAREN@16..17 "("
          NAME_REF@17..18
            IDENT@17..18 "a"
          COMMA@18..19 ","
          WHITESPACE@19..20 "\n"
          NAME_REF@20..21
            IDENT@20..21 "b"
  WHITESPACE@21..22 "\n"

error[DS0112]: unclosed `(`
  --> query:1:17
  |
1 | from T | where f(a,
  |                 ^ this `(` is never closed
2 | b
  |  - the input ends before a `)`
  |
  = help: add `)` where the bracketed part ends
